@startuml
' Why the corruption was permanent rather than a one-off: load re-materialised the
' phantom edge, so save wrote it back, so every later deploy failed.
title D1 — the self-perpetuating corruption loop

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #455A64
  LifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
  ParticipantBorderThickness 1.5
}

actor "Author" as U #ECEFF1
participant "Context menu\n<size:10>menuItems.tsx</size>" as MENU #FFF3E0
participant "React Flow\nstate" as RF #ECEFF1
participant "toApiGraph\n<size:10>graph.ts</size>" as SAVE #FFF3E0
database "Chain\n<size:10>team versions</size>" as CHAIN #E3F2FD
participant "fromApiGraph\n<size:10>graph.ts</size>" as LOAD #FFF3E0
participant "embers parse\n<size:10>Rust</size>" as PARSE #FFEBEE

== Fault introduced ==
U -> MENU : right-click → "Delete node"\n<size:10>observed: the ""Cavify"" node, wired ""Condense → Cavify → Output""</size>
MENU -> RF : onNodesChange([{id, type:"remove"}])
note right of RF #FFEBEE
  **applyNodeChanges removes the node only.**
  Its edges remain, now naming a vertex
  that no longer exists.
end note
RF --> U : node disappears — looks correct
note right of U #FFF3E0
  React Flow declines to draw an edge to a
  missing node, so nothing appears wrong.
  **No signal at the point of failure.**
end note

== Error committed to storage ==
U -> SAVE : Save
SAVE -> CHAIN : graphl with 9 contexts, 10 vertex ids
note right of CHAIN #FFEBEE
  Append-only: the ill-formed version is
  now permanent history.
end note

== The loop ==
U -> LOAD : reopen the team
CHAIN -> LOAD : graphl
LOAD -> RF : edges **including** the phantom
note right of LOAD #FFEBEE
  buildEdges did not check endpoints, so the
  phantom is read straight back in.
  <latex>s \circ l</latex> maps ill-formed to ill-formed —
  the corruption is a **fixed point**.
end note
U -> SAVE : Save again
SAVE -> CHAIN : the same ill-formed graph

== Failure, far from the cause ==
U -> PARSE : Deploy
PARSE --> U : ""node aae6cd19… is missing context""
note right of PARSE #FFEBEE
  First and only signal. Different process,
  opaque id, no node label, no hint that a
  stale edge is the cause.
end note

note over U, PARSE #E8F5E9
  **After the fix:** the menu delegates to React Flow's own
  ""deleteElements"", which removes connected edges with the node;
  load drops any edge naming an undefined vertex, so reopening and
  saving repairs the stored graph; and save refuses to emit one.
end note
@enduml
